  "narrative": {
    "intro": "AmerisourceBergen Drug is a major federal contractor with $6B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 19.9% year over year, and current-year totals are partial. The company recorded 385,562 awards, producing an average award size of $15.5K. Fiscal-year obligations climbed from $2.1B in FY21 and $2B in FY22 to $4.4B in FY23, then rose to $6.1B in FY24 and $7.4B in FY25 before landing at $6B so far in FY26. Department of Defense obligated $6B, making the Department of Defense the largest buying agency by obligations in FY2026 to date. Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $639K. Department of Justice obligated $28K. Medicinal and Botanical Manufacturing accounted for $4B in obligations. Drugs and Druggists' Sundries Merchant Wholesalers accounted for $2B. Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing accounted for $639K. The mix of large defense purchases and concentrated pharmaceutical manufacturing markets explains the high total obligations and the relatively low average award size. These figures reflect contract obligations rather than total contract values, and award-value tables may differ for largest awards or expiring contracts.",
